{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1445465","formula":"C₇H₇N₃O₂S","hill":"C7H7N3O2S","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":7.0,"N":3.0,"O":2.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"p-toluenesulfonyl azide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tosyl azide (systematic name: 4-methylbenzenesulfonyl azide; abbreviation: TsN3) is an organic compound with the formula CH3C6H4SO2N3. It is a widely used reagent in organic synthesis, primarily valued for its ability to transfer diazo groups and generate reactive nitrene intermediates. Although it is one of the more stable sulfonyl azides, it is highly energetic, heat- and shock-sensitive, and presents significant explosive hazards, particularly when isolated in pure bulk form."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":13661,"mass":197.22,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC=C(C=C1)S(=O)(=O)N=[N+]=[N-]","inchikey":"NDLIRBZKZSDGSO-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-diazo-4-methylbenzenesulfonamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"13661","atoms":20,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.684,"y":-0.876,"z":-0.201,"el":"S"},{"x":1.734,"y":-2.317,"z":0.106,"el":"O"},{"x":2.074,"y":-0.578,"z":-1.591,"el":"O"},{"x":2.448,"y":0.034,"z":0.884,"el":"N"},{"x":2.265,"y":1.45,"z":0.593,"el":"N"},{"x":2.133,"y":2.509,"z":0.384,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.009,"y":-0.461,"z":-0.115,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.716,"y":0.202,"z":0.024,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.519,"y":0.561,"z":-0.915,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.853,"y":-1.151,"z":0.756,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.872,"y":0.893,"z":-0.846,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.206,"y":-0.82,"z":0.825,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.163,"y":0.555,"z":0.097,"el":"C"},{"x":0.118,"y":1.116,"z":-1.599,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.477,"y":-1.945,"z":1.395,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.257,"y":1.69,"z":-1.476,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.853,"y":-1.365,"z":1.507,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.564,"y":0.371,"z":1.099,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.322,"y":1.617,"z":-0.122,"el"